{data-component="concept-intro"}
::::
{.eyebrow .annot}
[← watershed](/) · Component model

# Give users\
_the parts._

{.lede}
These sheets answer one question: what if the user, not the author, decides what is on the page? The running example is a shared board: build it out of parts, wire it up, and save its arrangement in a workspace within the shared document.

{.lede}
Skip this section if your application ships a screen you lay out yourself. Start with [the foundations](/foundations) for the document model every watershed app uses.
::::

{data-component="concept-content"}
:::::
{data-heading-id="fh-ledger-title"}
## Component model

{.fh-scope .annot .fh-scope-optional}
Optional · user-constructable apps

3 sheets. One example board, built, wired, and saved. The first two split in half: using the parts, then writing one.

{data-component="concept-aside"}
:::
Need a fixed application screen instead? Return to [the foundations](/foundations), then follow [the survey procedure](/guide).
:::
